<h2>Requirement description</h2>

<p>
This requirement is concerned with ensuring that significant architecture decisions are documented, understood and traceable.
</p>

<p>
Architecture decisions should not be stored solely in emails, meeting notes or individual knowledge. The reasoning behind decisions should be recorded, including the options considered, trade-offs assessed and rationale for the selected approach.
</p>

<p>
The objective is to ensure future teams can understand why decisions were made, challenge assumptions where necessary and avoid repeatedly analysing the same problems.
</p>

<p>
<strong>In simple terms:</strong><br>
Important architecture decisions should be documented in a consistent format that explains what was decided, what alternatives were considered and why the decision was taken.
</p>

