<h2>What assessors should look for</h2>

<ol>
<li>
<strong>Decision coverage</strong> – Are significant architecture decisions formally documented?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Options analysis</strong> – Do records show alternative approaches that were considered?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Decision rationale</strong> – Is the reasoning behind decisions clearly explained?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Consistency</strong> – Are decisions recorded using a repeatable format or template?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Maintainability</strong> – Are decision records maintained and accessible to the delivery team?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Traceability</strong> – Can decisions be linked to architecture artefacts, governance activities, requirements, risks or standards?
</li>
</ol>

<h2>What separates a 3 from a 4 or 5</h2>

<p>
A score of <strong>3</strong> typically means that many significant decisions are documented and rationale is generally available, but coverage is incomplete or the quality of records varies between decisions.
</p>

<p>
A score of <strong>4</strong> requires a consistent and maintained ADR approach. Most significant decisions are recorded, alternatives are documented and decision records can be traced to governance and architecture artefacts.
</p>

<p>
A score of <strong>5</strong> requires ADRs to be embedded within the delivery lifecycle. Decision records are routinely created, maintained and actively used to support governance, future design work, technical debt management and architecture evolution.
</p>

<h2>Suggested evidence examples (not SAF-mandated artefacts)</h2>

<ul>
<li>Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)</li>
<li>SEQF Any Decision Record templates</li>
<li>Decision logs or registers</li>
<li>Architecture repository entries</li>
<li>Design Authority outputs linked to ADRs</li>
<li>Governance review records referencing decisions</li>
<li>Solution Design Overview documents referencing ADRs</li>
<li>Architecture roadmaps linked to decisions</li>
<li>Technical debt records referencing prior decisions</li>
<li>Knowledge repositories containing maintained decision records</li>
</ul>


